Timsort is a sorting algorithm that is similar to the popular Timsort algorithm, but it is designed to be more efficient and scalable. It is a hybrid sorting algorithm that combines the best features of quicksort and heapsort.

Here is an example of how you can implement Timsort in Lean 4:
```
import lean4.sorting

// Define the Timsort algorithm
def timsort[A](arr: Array[A]): Array[A] = {
  // Create a new array to hold the sorted elements
  val sorted = new Array[A](arr.length)

  // Partition the array into two subarrays
  // using the median of three pivot elements
  val mid = arr.length / 2
  val left = arr.take(mid).toArray
  val right = arr.drop(mid).toArray

  // Sort the left subarray using heapsort
  timsort(left)

  // Sort the right subarray using quicksort
  timsort(right)

  // Merge the sorted subarrays
  sorted.zip(left).foreach { case (a, b) => sorted :+ a }
  sorted.zip(right).foreach { case (a, b) => sorted :+ b }

  sorted
}
```
The Timsort algorithm works by first partitioning the array into two subarrays using the median of three pivot elements. It then sorts each subarray using a different sorting algorithm (heapsort for the left subarray and quicksort for the right subarray). Finally,

